   "id": "l13",
   "number": "13",
   "title": "Design that persuades",
   "kicker": "Graphic design and public messages",
   "lead": "Graphic design is art with a deadline and a client. It is also the visual grammar of everything you read on a screen.",
   "body": [
    "Constructivism builds a poster like a machine part: red, black, diagonal, photograph cut against geometry. Bauhaus reduces to elementary shapes on a grid and lowercase type. Art Deco streamlines the same geometry into luxury. Swiss Style adds the grid we still use. Pop Art collapses fine art and advertising by using the advert's own printing method. Psychedelic posters warp type until legibility becomes a trip. Memphis and Space Age design are period flavour, and Afrofuturism shows the same design vocabulary turned toward a future worth wanting.",
    "Learn this lesson with a ruler. Almost every rule here is arithmetic."
   ],
   "takeaway": "Design is the art of deciding what to leave out on purpose.",
